====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# Newly [[produced]] or [[obtained]]; [[recent]].
#: {{ux|en|He followed the '''fresh''' hoofprints to find the deer.}}
#: {{ux|en|I seem to make '''fresh''' mistakes every time I start writing.}}
#: {{ux|en|With his recent divorce still '''fresh''' in his mind, he was unable to concentrate on his work.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=You have heard of Them|editor=D. W. Holly|journal=The United States Review|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Lloyd & Brainard{{nb...|Publishers and Proprietors. 80 Nassau-Street.}}|month=October|year=1854|page=327|passage=Where will you find a purer and more suggestive bit of criticism given in a '''fresher''' and more implicatory style than the following?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Steve Thorngate|title=Morice-Brubaker takes on Douthat|titleurl=http://www.christiancentury.org/blogs/archive/2012-07/morice-brubaker-takes-douthat|journal=The Christian Century|date=17 July 2012
|passage=Ross Douthat's gotten a lot of pushback for using his soapbox to complain that liberal Christianity lacks "a religious reason for its own existence." And with good reason—it'd be nice if the national paper of record's faithiest columnist could at least spin a '''fresher''' argument against us mainliners.}}
# (''of [[food]]'') Not [[dried]], [[frozen]], or [[spoiled]].
#: {{ant|en|stale}}
#: {{ux|en|After taking a beating in the boxing ring, the left side of his face looked like '''fresh''' meat.}}
#: {{ux|en|I brought home from the market a nice bunch of '''fresh''' spinach leaves straight from the farm.}}
#: {{ux|en|a glass of '''fresh''' milk}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Catherine Hanger|title=Morocco: World Food|passage=In fact, street food may well be '''fresher''' than that served in restaurants and cafes, as it is cooked at the point of sale. It's certainly much cheaper.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Darcy Encarnacion|title=When It Falls|journal=Scribbles|url=https://issuu.com/wgdlsu/docs/scribbles_volume_i_issue_1_-_september_2020__final|volume=1|issue=1|location=Manila|publisher={{w|De La Salle University}} Writers’ Guild|date=2020-09|page=14|passage=The ravenette smiled. Today was her little sister’s birthday, and what better way to commemorate than eating salad brimmed with the '''freshest''' of fruits. Following Tala, Amihan felt her heart sore. Luscious short brown hair, almond-shaped eyes, gleaming smiles, there is no one as extravagant as her beloved, Bagwis.}}
# {{lb|en|botany}} (''of [[plant material]]'') Still [[green]] and not [[dried]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii
|passage=With '''fresh''' material, taxonomic conclusions are leavened by recognition that the material examined reflects the site it occupied; a herbarium packet gives one only a small fraction of the data desirable for sound conclusions. Herbarium material does not, indeed, allow one to extrapolate safely: what you see is what you get{{...}}}}
# [[invigorating|Invigoratingly]] [[cool]] and [[refreshing]].
#: {{syn|en|cool}}
#: {{ux|en|What a nice '''fresh''' breeze.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=The English Girl|author=Margaret Leroy|page=|ISBN=1405525576|passage=The corridor stinks of sweat and cigarette smoke, and I daringly open the window a little. The '''freshest''' air floats in, smelling of sappy grasses, the delicate pollens of wild flowers, the resins of the pine forests; hinting at the chill blue scent of distant snows. }}
# (''of [[water]]'') Without [[salt]]; not [[saline]].
#: {{ant|en|saline}}
#: {{ux|en|After a day at sea it was good to feel the '''fresh''' water of the stream.}}
#* {{ante|1628}}, [[w:Sir Francis Drake|Sir Francis Drake]](?), ''The World Encompassed'', Nicholas Bourne (publisher, 1628), [http://books.google.com/books?id=BDwFAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA168&dq=fresh page 49]:
#*: {{quote|en|There we made our ſhip faſt with foure ropes, in ſmooth water, and the '''freſh''' water ranne downe out of the hill into the ſea, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1820|author=William Scoresby|title=An Account of the Arctic Regions|publisher=Archibald Constable & Co.|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=d77RAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA230&dq=fresh|page=230
|passage=When dissolved, it produces water sometimes perfectly '''fresh''', and sometimes saltish; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Adele Pillitteri|title=Maternal and Child Health Nursing|publisher=Sixth Edition, Lippincott Williams & Wilkins|isbn=9781582559995|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=apeLf0mPx1QC&pg=PA1557&dq=fresh|page=1557
|passage=Additional changes that occur when water enters the lungs depend on whether the water is '''fresh''' or salt.}}
# [[rested|Rested]]; not [[tired]] or [[fatigued]].
#: {{syn|en|rested}}
#: {{ant|en|tired}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2010|author=Sam Sheringham|title=Liverpool 0 - 1 Wolverhampton|work=BBC|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9308904.stm
|passage=Before the match, Hodgson had expressed the hope that his players would be '''fresh''' rather than rusty after an 18-day break from league commitments because of two successive postponements.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230110155247/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9308904.stm|archivedate=10 January 2023}}
# In a [[raw]] or [[untried]] state; [[uncultured]]; [[unpracticed]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:inexperienced}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''fresh''' hand on a ship}}
# [[youthful|Youthful]]; [[florid]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|IV|i|passage=these '''fresh''' nymphs}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[good|Good]], [[fashionable]].
#: {{syn|en|cool|fashionable}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''fresh''' pair of sneakers}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Fresh|album=Emergency| artist=Kool & the Gang| year=1984| passage=I've been thinking about the way you walk <br> Baby ooh I like the way you talk <br> Tell you something I really can't hide <br> Heaven must have sent you to be by my side <br> '''Fresh''' and lovely '''fresh''' like a dream come true <br> I'll give anything to spend the night with you}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1988|title={{w|Supersonic (J. J. Fad song)|Supersonic}}|artist=w:J. J. Fad|passage=Because my devastating beats I know you will like / You see my beat box is '''fresh''', it'll blow your mind}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|slang}} [[tipsy|Tipsy]]; [[drunk]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1840|title=Parliamentary Papers|volume=9|page=43
|passage=How long did Mr. Crisp stay with you?—He might have stayed two hours; he stayed some time after; he drank ale and got '''fresh'''.}}

