{{en-noun}}

# A [[rush]] of [[water]], along a river or onto the land; a [[flood]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1834|author=David Crockett|title=A Narrative of the Life of David Crockett|location=Nebraska|year_published=1987|page=21
|passage=They went on very well with their work until it was nigh done, when there came the second epistle to Noah's '''fresh''', and away went their mill, shot, lock, and barrel.}}
# A [[stream]] or [[spring]] of fresh water.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|III|ii|text={{...}}And take his bottle from him. / When that's gone, / He shall drink naught but brine, for I'll not show him / Where the quick '''freshes''' are.}}
# The mingling of fresh water with salt in rivers or bays, as by means of a flood of fresh water flowing toward or into the sea.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=History and Present State of Virginia|author=w:Robert Beverley, Jr.|year=1705|passage=When they cross any great Water, or violent '''Fresh''', or Torrent, they throw Tobacco, Puccoon, Peak, or some other valuable thing, that they happen to have about there, to intreat the Spirit presiding there, to grant them a safe passage. It is call'd a '''Fresh''', when after very great Rains, or (as we suppose) after a great Thaw of the Snow and Ice lying upon the Mountains Page 43 to the North West, the Water descends, in such abundance into the Rivers, that they overflow the Banks which bound their Streams at other times.}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|commercial|fishing}} To pack (fish) loosely on [[ice]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1921|title=Report - Volume 12  |author=Commonwealth Shipping Committee |page=|ISBN=|passage=With the exception of about 1800 crans which were "rough packed," all the herrings landed during the winter months were '''freshed''' and kippered.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1960|title=Lord of the Isles: Lord Leverhulme of the Hebrides |author=Nigel Nicolson |page=84|ISBN=|passage=Aided by government propaganda, herring became an important British war-time food, not pickled, but ''''freshed'''' (packed loosely in ice) and kippered. }}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1971 |title=Marine Products in Japan: Size, Technology and Research |author=Eiichi Tanikawa |page=189|ISBN=|passage=Smoked abalone is prepared by smoking the salted and '''freshed''' abalone, the smoked meat is packed with vegetable oil.}}
# To [[flood]] or [[dilute]] an area of [[salt water]] with flowing [[fresh water]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1974|title=Bilješke - Volumes 31-76 |author=|page=1|ISBN=|passage=Our first assumption was that '''freshed''' sea water areas were favourable for these organisms.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1977 |title=Lok Sabha Debates |author=India. Parliament. House of the People, India. Parliament. Lok Sabha |page=226|ISBN=|passage=Under the present river conditions, headwater discharge of 40,000 cusecs will be necessary during the non-'''freshed''' season to neutralise the landward drift of sediments throughout the tidal portion of the river.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1987 |title=Equal Rites |author=Terry Pratchett |page=69|ISBN=0552131059|passage=But as the golden light flowed slowly across the Discworld like the first '''freshing''' of the tide over mudflats the eagle circled higher into the dome of heaven, beating the air down with slow and powerful wingbeats.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1989 |title=Developments in geoscience |author=Tseng-chʻüan Li; Fa-erh Chiang; Shu Sun |page=325|ISBN=|passage=The salinity is variated, and locally the lake water is '''freshed''' in a step manner.}}
# {{lb|en|of wind}} To become [[strong]]er.
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1815|title=The Journal of Llewellin Penrose, a Seaman|author=William Williams |page=|ISBN=|passage=Horrible was now my condition, as the wind '''freshed''' up more and more.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1834 |title=The naval officer |author=Frederick Marryat |page=259|ISBN=|passage=I should have observed, that as we rounded the north-east point, the breeze '''freshed''', and the squalls came heavy out of the gullies and deep ravines.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1850|title=An Attempt to Develop the Law of Storms by Means of Facts|author=William Reid |page=|ISBN=|passage=On the afternoon of the 20th, at the period the storm was very severe to the south-west of her, the Barlow experienced calms and variable winds. By noon on the 21st, the wind '''freshed''', with the weather cloudy.}}
# To [[rebore]] the [[barrel]] of a [[rifle]] or [[shotgun]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1910|title=Hunter-trader-trapper - Volume 19, Issue 6 |author=|page=92|ISBN=|passage=When the barrel became very rough the gun was taken to the local gunsmith and "'''freshed'''."}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1974|title=Home guide to muzzle-loaders |author=George C. Nonte |page=132|ISBN=0811721019|passage=There is also the oft-heard plaint that "modern steel barrels can't be re-rifled or '''freshed''' out." }}
# To [[update]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1822|title=Life of ―, a scotish govenanter |author=Alexander Reid |page=7|ISBN=|passage=Thus the liberties of the nation, civil and religious, were laid '''freshed''' by his preaching, and. more and more confirmed in the presbyterian principles: and we likewise resorted for a time at West Calder kirk, to Mr. Patrick Shiels, by whose preaching I was yet more confirmed in the presbyterian way.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1885|title=Chinese Recorder - Volume 16 |author=|page=419|ISBN=|passage=We need not assume that the famous village was considered the capital of the country spoken of; it is sufficient to know that the priests who '''freshed''' up the old Ta-ts'in lore in China, were proud of having been themselves born in the Holy Land; and if we consider the precedent set in the very ''T'ang-shu'', where the whole of India is designated by the name of Buddha's birth place, Magadha, we need not be astonished to see the name of what they must have considered the spiritual capital of the Christian world applied to the country they came from.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2000|title=Jesus Outside the New Testament: An Introduction to the Ancient Evidence |author=Robert Van Voorst; Craig A. Evans; Bruce Chilton |page=122|ISBN=0802843689|passage=The strongest judgment against the ''Toledot Yeshu'' was made by Solomon Schechter in 1898, "All the so-called Anti-Christiana collected by medieval [Jewish] fanatics, and '''freshed''' up again by modern ignoramuses, belong to the later centuries, when history and biography had already given way to myth and speculation."}}
# To [[freshen up]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1943|title=Maggie No Doubt |author=Maggie Jeanne Melody Wadelton |page=132|ISBN=|passage=I '''freshed''' meself and followed after him and made choice of me dinner.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2009|title=The Great Hunt|author=Robert Jordan |page=|ISBN=0748115358|passage=There was no need for them all to be there—most would be resting in their rooms, '''freshing''' from the journey—but she was on edge now, all the questions she could not ask running through her head.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2012 |title=First Lady: A Hood Tale |author=Mz. K. |page=116|ISBN=1469159503|passage=We played and adored our boys, we watched a little television until about six, I got a shower and put my clothes back on I got the boys '''freshed''' up while Aj was in the shower and he got dressed.}}
# To [[renew]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1884|title=United States Congressional Serial Set - Volume 2178 |author=|page=503|ISBN=|passage=Q. Did you tell anybody this tale that you heard this man threaten what they were going to do?—A. No, sir; I didn't say nothing to anybody until Monday—Monday or Tuesday, one—then my mind was '''freshed'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1902|title=Down-adown-derry: A Book of Fairy Poems|author=Walter De la Mare; Dorothy Pulis Lathrop |page=|ISBN=1465525696|passage=In the nook of a wood where a pool '''freshed''' with dew Glassed, daybreak till evening, blue sky glimpsing through Then a star; or a slip of May-moon silver-white, Thridding softly aloof the quiet of night, Was a thicket of flowers. }}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1918|title=The Indian Forest Records - Volume 6, Parts 1-6 |author=|page=316|ISBN=|passage=About a month later, the blaze is '''freshed''' by cutting off a thin shaving of bark all round the stem, over half the depth of the old blaze and taking in 2 inches of new bark on the upper edge of the original wound.}}
# {{lb|en|farming|zoology}} Of a [[dairy cow]], to [[give birth]] to a [[calf]].
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1940 |title=The cow tester's manual |author=James Frank Kendrick |page=23|ISBN=|passage=A cow was actually tested twice a month on the 5th and 25th of each month. The cow '''freshed''' December 15, her milk was good December 18, and she went dry October 30.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=1946|title=Co-op News – Volumes 20-21 |author=|page=3|ISBN=|passage=Fall '''Freshed''' Cows Produce More Milk.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2009|title=Amish Peace: Simple Wisdom for a Complicated World |author=Suzanne Woods Fisher |page=56|ISBN=1441210881|passage=On the day of my visit, Mary greets me at my car with a delighted look on her face. “You're just in time!” she says eagerly. “A cow has just ''''freshed''''!”}}

