===Etymology 2===
First use appears c. 1848, US slang, probably from {{bor|en|de|frech|t=impudent, cheeky, insolent}}, from {{der|en|gmh|vrech|t=bold, brave, lively}}, from {{der|en|goh|freh|t=greedy, eager, avaricious, covetous}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*frek}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*frekaz|t=greedy, outrageous, courageous, capable, active}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*preg-|t=to be quick, twitch, sprinkle, splash}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|frec|t=greedy; eager, bold, daring; dangerous}} and {{cog|da|fræk|t=naughty}}. More at {{l|en|freak}}.

