===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[cover]] of [[minute]] [[ice]] [[crystal]]s on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as [[dew]], except that the [[temperature]] of the frosted object is below [[freezing]].
# The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Genesis|chapter=31|verse=40|passage=Thus I was; in the day the drought consumed me, and the '''frost''' by night; and my sleep departed from mine eyes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1748|author=David Hume|title=Enquiries concerning the human understanding and concerning the principles of moral.|location=London|publisher=Oxford University Press|year_published=1973|section=§ 47
|passage=It is more probable, in almost every country of Europe, that there will be '''frost''' sometime in January, than that the weather will continue open throughout that whole month;}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Coldness or insensibility; severity or rigidity of character.
#* {{RQ:Scott Guy Mannering|passage=It was one of those moments of intense feeling when the '''frost''' of the Scottish people melts like a snow-wreath.}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Max Carrados Mysteries|passage=Up to that time the girl had never really done her hair, and she regarded boots merely as things to protect the feet. Suddenly it dawned on her that she was considered plain and that she diffused an atmosphere of intellectual '''frost'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Josh Halliday|title=Prince Harry may cancel UK family visit after being refused police protection|work=The Guardian|date=2026-06-28|url=https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jun/28/prince-harry-uk-family-visit-refused-police-protection|issn=0261-3077|passage=An LA-based business associate of Harry and Meghan, who live in Montecito, California, told the Telegraph there had been a “warming of the '''frost'''” between the king and his youngest son after Harry’s public attacks in his memoir, Spare, and television interviews.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of [[freeze|freezing]]; the [[congelation]] of [[water]] or other liquid.
# A shade of white, like that of frost.
#: {{color panel|ECFCFC}}
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} A [[disappointment]]; a [[cheat]].
# {{lb|en|television}} A kind of [[light]] [[diffuser]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Alan Bermingham|title=Location Lighting for Television|pages=9–26
|passage='''Frosts''' and diffusion are flame retardant and produce similar results except that some of the '''frosts''' are very subtle in their effects. For example: Hamburg '''Frost''' will soften the beam edge with little additional spread of the beam.}}

