# {{lb|en|ice hockey}} An umbrella term for a [[centre]] or [[winger]] in [[ice hockey]].
# {{lb|en|basketball}} The small forward or power forward position; two [[frontcourt]] positions that are taller than guards but shorter than centers.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The front part of a [[vessel]].
# {{lb|en|Internet}} An [[e-mail]] message that is forwarded to another recipient or recipients; an electronic [[chain letter]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Tamara Stevens|title=What Is Snail Mail?: The Lost Art of Letterwriting|page=27
|passage=When you receive your new pen-pal's email address, do not automatically put it in your address book and use the email Addy to send ''''forwards'''' to. Not every pen pal likes 'forwards', especially jokes and meaningless emails.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Joli Ballew|title=Windows 7 for the Over 50s in Simple Steps|passage=This method attaches the files to a new email, which is fine if you want to create a new email. The only problem with this is that it doesn't work if you'd rather send '''forwards''' or replies.}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} A direct agreement between two parties to buy or sell an [[asset]] at a specific point in the [[future]]; distinguished from a [[futures contract]] in that the latter is [[standardize]]d and traded on an [[exchange]].
#: {{synonyms|en|forward contract}}
