====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# Extreme [[anger]].
#* {{RQ:Congreve Mourning Bride|page=39|passage=Heav'n has no Rage, like Love to Hatred turn'd, / Nor Hell a '''Fury''', like a Woman ſcorn'd.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=March|author=J. P. Wilson; E. N. C. Haywood|title=The route through the Peak - Derby to Manchester: Part One|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=155|text=The building of the railway in this notable beauty spot roused the great Victorian writer {{w|John Ruskin}} to '''fury'''.}}
# [[strength|Strength]] or [[violence]] in action.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Lucrece|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=SjYOAQAAMAAJ&pg=PT38|passage=Small lightes are ſoone blown out, huge fires abide, / And with the winde in greater '''furie''' fret: / The petty ſtreames that paie a dailie [[debt|det]] / To their ſalt ſoveraigne with their freſh [[falls|fals]] [[haste|haſt]], / Adde to his flowe, but alter not his [[tast|taſt]].}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|VI|passage=I don't mean all of your friends—only a small proportion—which, however, connects your circle with that deadly, idle, brainless bunch—the insolent chatterers at the opera,{{...}}the speed-mad fugitives from the '''furies''' of ennui, the neurotic victims of mental cirrhosis,{{nb...}}!}}
# An [[angry]] or [[malignant]] person.

